LGPL-2.1-or-later; see LICENSE. Other project-authored adapters, native bridges,
build recipes, and packaging tools remain LGPL-2.1-or-later. The stable client header remains ISC so
independent proprietary or open-source applications can implement an adapter.
VideoLAN VLC, its plugins, and every transitive native dependency retain
their upstream terms. A release is eligible only when its exact binary graph,
licenses, notices, source offer, and hashes pass the repository compliance
policy.
